<title>JAPAN: Japan April industrial output down revised 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan April industrial output down revised 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in April fell a revised 0.5 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 0.4 percent fall, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year basis, industrial production in April rose a revised 4.8 percent, against a preliminary estimate of a 4.9 percent increase.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  APR     PRELIM    MONTH AGO APRINDEX</p>
<p> Output		 -0.5    -0.4    -0.3    100.7</p>
<p> Shipments	    -2.8    -2.4    +0.8    101.5</p>
<p> Inventories	  +3.1    +2.9    -2.7    106.5</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   +8.0    +7.2    -3.5    114.7</p>
<p>Capacity utilisation</p>
<p>rate		    -0.1    N.A.    +0.7     89.3</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>			  APR     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output		 +4.8    +7.6</p>
<p> Shipments	    +4.4    +9.0</p>
<p> Inventories	  -2.2    -5.5</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   -1.9   -11.2</p>
<p>Capacity utilisation</p>
<p>rate		    +4.5    +6.1</p>
